## 4. File Change Summary Tables

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/store/chats.js` | Modify | `actions.setActiveChat` | Removed the legacy `if (!$storex.ui.isDesktopMode) → navigation.chats.open(...)` route branch and the duplicate panel branch. Now loads the chat, sets `activeChatId`, then opens it exactly once through the unified `$storex.ui.openChat(chat)` (panel on desktop / route on mobile). Kept the desktop “vibe” guard so vibe mode doesn’t force a panel. |
| `src/store/ui.js` | Modify | `actions.openApp` | Uses the Vuex `(context, payload)` contract and accepts a bare key (`'wiki'`) or `{ appKey, payload }`, forwarding to `navigation.openApp`. This is what lets `openChat` (and therefore `setActiveChat`) reach the unified opener on **both** modes, including the `codx-junior-split` desktop route where the old branch was skipped. |
| `src/store/ui.js` | Modify | `mutations.openChat`, `mutations.openFileInViewer`, `actions.openTeamChannel/DM/MediaLibrary`, `actions.openWorkspace/openMeet/openTutorial` | Pass payloads in the `{ appKey, payload }` object form so Vuex’s single-payload dispatch doesn’t drop the chat / file / team data. |
| `src/store/ui.js` | Modify | `mutations.setActiveTab`, `mutations.showTab` | Unify tab opening through `openApp` (fixes aliased keys such as `planning`) — keeps every `$ui.setActiveTab('<appKey>')` launcher working on desktop and mobile. |

---

## 4. Verification Checklist

- [ ] **Desktop (route `codx-junior-split`)** → click any chat / `setActiveChat` → the chat **panel opens** (this was the failing path: old code skipped the route branch and relied on `openChat`, which only works with the fixed `openApp`).
- [ ] **Desktop (any other route)** → chat opens as a panel **once** (no duplicate panels; dedup by `chat-<id>` key preserved).
- [ ] **Mobile** → `setActiveChat` navigates to `/chats/:chatId/:chatName`.
- [ ] Threads: `ChatEntry.openThread` → `setActiveChat(threadChat)` opens correctly on both modes.
- [ ] Kanban / Wall: `Kanban.setActiveChat`, `Wall.setActiveChat`, `ChatHistory.openChat` all still open the chat.
- [ ] `createNewChatFromUrl`, `createNewBoardChat`, `createNewThread` still activate the created chat.
- [ ] Terminal shows **no** `[UI] openApp: missing app key` / `[Navigation] openApp: unknown app "…"` warnings.
- [ ] Desktop “vibe” mode: no unexpected chat panel is forced open.

> Note: the `openApp` action must keep the `(context, payload)` signature — Vuex always injects the action context as the first argument. `setActiveChat` depends on this via `openChat`.

